@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+# Paper 2 · Detection matrix
+
+Built 2026-10-20 by `9-Paper2/build_detection_matrix.py` from the committed result files.
+Outputs: `5-Results/paper2__detection-matrix.csv`, `5-Results/paper2__burst-check.csv`.
+
+**Question:** for each leak mechanism and each dataset, is the leak present, does paper 1's
+nine-question checklist (v1) flag it, and what does it cost?
+**Effect:** XGBoost ROC-AUC, leaky configuration vs its fair comparator, as the range over the splits run.
+
+## The matrix
+
+| Mechanism | Checklist v1 | Retail Rocket | Flower shop | REES46 (clean) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **L1** A count reconstructs the label | Q4 | present (exact); **flagged**; 1.00 vs 0.61–0.62 | absent (identity holds in 0% of sessions); **correctly not flagged** | approximate (= purchases + removals); **partly flagged**; 0.91 vs 0.72–0.73 |
+| **L2** Completed-session timing | Q5, Q6 | present; **flagged**; 0.995 vs 0.61–0.62 | present; **flagged**; 0.76–0.78 vs 0.58–0.62 | present; **flagged**; 0.96 vs 0.72–0.73 |
+| **L3** Label mixes purchase and abandonment | Q3 | present; **flagged**; 11.3% of purchased sessions | present (small); **flagged**; 3 of 320 | present; **flagged**; 722 of 18,560 (3.9%) |
+| **L4** History includes the scored purchase | none | present; **missed**; 0.97–0.98 vs 0.68–0.71 | present; **missed**; 0.93–0.94 vs 0.59–0.61 | present; **missed**; 0.89–0.90 vs 0.56 |
+| **L5** History includes later purchases | none | weak; **missed**; 0.68–0.73 vs 0.68–0.71 | present; **missed**; 0.67–0.69 vs 0.59–0.61 | present; **missed**; 0.60–0.62 vs 0.56 |
+| **L6** Checkout steps after the prediction moment | none | not logged | present; **missed**; 0.83–0.87 vs 0.58–0.62 | not logged |
+| **L7** Automated traffic past the bot filter | none | absent (burst check) | absent (burst check) | present; **missed**; 0.59–0.66 vs 0.50–0.54 (first add, visitor split) |
+
+How each leak entered the data: L1 and L2 come from paper 1's own feature function, the way a typical session table is built. L4–L6 are features built the way a routine pipeline would build them ("lifetime purchases", "item conversion rate", checkout-step counts). L7 sits in the raw data. L3 is a property of the label (an item-level share, no AUC effect measured).
+
+## What it shows
+
+- **Checklist v1 catches the leaks it was written for, on every new dataset.** L2 and L3 are flagged on 3 of 3 datasets. L1 is flagged where it exists exactly, correctly not flagged where it doesn't (flower shop), and only partly caught where it exists approximately (REES46).
+- **It misses every leak outside its scope**, and those include the largest one: L4 (self-inclusion) reaches 0.89–0.98 on all three datasets with no question pointing at it.
+- **Count over the 16 cases where a leak is present:** flagged 7, partly flagged 1, missed 8.
+- **False positives:** no question raised a flag where no leak existed. With only one true negative in the matrix (L1 on the flower shop), a false-positive *rate* can't be estimated yet.
+
+## Burst check (L7), applied to all three datasets
+
+Cart sessions per day; a day is flagged above 1.5× the median daily count.
+
+| | Flagged days | Purchase rate, flagged vs other | Night share (00–06), flagged vs other | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Retail Rocket | 1 (2015-06-16) | 31% vs 27% | 27% vs 29% | busy day, not automated |
+| Flower shop | 6 (occasion days, Sep–Oct) | 30% vs 35% | 5% vs 6% | busy days, not automated |
+| REES46 | 5 (Oct 1, 2, 6, 7, 8) | **6% vs 16%** | **20% vs 10%** | automated traffic |
+
+Rule for "present": flagged days whose purchase rate is below 60% of the other days'. The night share confirms it independently.
+
+## Proposed checklist v2 (to be tested on unseen data)
+
+| # | Question | Covers |
+|---|---|---|
+| Q4′ | Can the label event's count be reconstructed from other counts, **exactly or approximately**? | L1 near-identities (REES46) |
+| Q10 | Does any feature record a step of the process that produces the label (checkout, payment) **after the prediction moment**? | L6 |
+| Q11 | Is any aggregate (customer history, item popularity) computed over a window that **includes the scored case or anything after the prediction moment**? | L4, L5 |
+| Q12 | Do daily volumes and the hour-of-day profile show **traffic the bot filter can't see** (bursts with flat days and low purchase rates)? | L7 |
+| Q13 | Did the **logging schema change** during the data period? | observed on the flower shop (Aug 23); not measured |
+
+**Circularity:** these questions were suggested by the same three datasets. Validating them needs data they weren't derived from (planned: REES46 November 2019).
+
+## Caveats
+- Flower-shop effects rest on 828 sessions (intervals about ±0.09); REES46 intervals are about ±0.01.
+- Retail Rocket's L4/L5 values come from the Oct 2 probe (printed values recorded in `docs/point_in_time_log.md`), not from a rerun in this repo.
+- The burst rule is simple and day-level; the 1.5× and 60% thresholds were set after seeing REES46 and need testing on unseen data too.
